# Optional. Copy to ".env" only if you want to override defaults.
#
# Operator runs through the Claude Agent SDK, which uses your existing Claude
# Code login automatically — so you usually need NOTHING here to get started.
#
# Set a model override (default is claude-sonnet-4-6; opus is more powerful/costly):
# OPERATOR_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
#
# If you'd rather run on a raw Anthropic API key instead of your Claude login:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# Where your Obsidian vault lives (offer, brand voice, People/ notes). Operator
# READS this as its source of truth; it never edits your notes. Default:
# ~/Documents/Obsidian Vault.
# OPERATOR_VAULT=/path/to/your/Obsidian Vault
#
# --- LinkedIn connect-vetting (opt-in, OFF by default) ------------------------
# When set, Operator may VET + LOG connection-request candidates (verified ICP,
# no note) and hand you the batch to send yourself — it never clicks Connect;
# the browser bridge stays read-only. Comments and DMs always stay draft-only.
# Leave unset for assist-only.
# OPERATOR_LINKEDIN_CONNECT=1
# Daily cap on approved connection requests (your norm is 50-100/day; start conservative):
# OPERATOR_LINKEDIN_DAILY_CAP=50
#
# --- Browser bridge: let Operator READ LinkedIn (read-only) -------------------
# Operator can read LinkedIn (profiles, posts, the feed) through a standalone
# Playwright-MCP browser server. It's READ-ONLY by design: the permission gate
# allows only read tools and denies every click/type/submit tool, so Operator can
# never connect, comment, DM, or post through it — you do all sending by hand.
#
# To turn it on (in a separate terminal, keep it running):
#   npx -y @playwright/mcp@latest --port 8931 --browser chrome \
#     --user-data-dir ~/.operator-linkedin-profile
# A Chrome window opens; log into LinkedIn ONCE there (the profile dir persists the
# session). Then point Operator at it:
# OPERATOR_CHROME_MCP_URL=http://localhost:8931/mcp
# Use the legacy SSE endpoint instead? Set the transport and use /sse:
# OPERATOR_CHROME_MCP_TRANSPORT=sse   (then URL = http://localhost:8931/sse)
#
# Leave unset to run without live LinkedIn access (paste content in instead).
